It follows that Wab (x) = Wab (Λ(x), p(x)) =\n\nL−1 (Λp) ΛL(p) ab, with a standard Lorentz transform (LT) Lab (p) deﬁned by,\n\nL00 (p) = γ, L0i (p) = Li0 (p) =\n\npi m\n\n,\n\npipk |−→p |2\n\nLik (p) = δik + (γ − 1)\n\n, (19)\n\n",
